        <type>bool</type>
        <definition>bool UTryllKvResidencyPolicy::bEnabled</definition>
        <argsstring></argsstring>
        <name>bEnabled</name>
        <qualifiedname>UTryllKvResidencyPolicy::bEnabled</qualifiedname>
        <initializer>= true</initializer>
        <briefdescription>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Whether the policy evicts at all. When false nothing is evicted, so toggling at runtime is safe; call RestoreAll afterwards to warm what was evicted.</para>
<para>Agents created with DeferAllocation stay that way — creation mode is structural. Turning the policy off mid-session restores what it evicted; it cannot undo an allocation that never happened. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
